#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lem — one CLI over lemlist.

Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by lemlist S.A.S.
"lemlist" is a trademark of lemlist S.A.S.

Three surfaces behind one entry point:

  lem rest ...        the official `@lemlist-official/cli` (REST, 143 operations).
                      We delegate — we do not reimplement it.
  lem mcp ...         lemlist's MCP action surface (124 tools), driven as plain
                      commands. Covers what REST does not: domain purchase and
                      mailbox provisioning, deliverability audits, inbox placement
                      tests, AI variable prompts, campaign folders, business
                      context. No MCP client needed, no 271 KB of tool schemas
                      loaded into an agent's context.
  lem dump-all ...    our resumable, GET-only tenant snapshot. Unchanged in spirit
                      from v0.2, but now driven off the *live* OpenAPI spec
                      instead of a vendored copy that goes stale.

Quick start:
  export LEMLIST_API_KEY=...
  lem doctor                       # check the toolchain end to end
  lem rest campaigns list          # anything the official CLI can do
  lem mcp tools --reads            # the read-only MCP surface
  lem mcp call get_team_info
  lem dump-all ../lemlist-data     # read-only snapshot, resumable

Safety:
  `lem rest` inherits the official CLI's own DELETE guard.
  `lem mcp call` refuses any non-read-only tool without --yes, and refuses the
  billing/irreversible ones without --force-danger on top.
  `lem dump-all` only ever issues GET (plus two documented read-only POST
  searches under --with-search). It cannot mutate your tenant.
"""
